## 8. Shared memory and state

The project's memory **lives in the repository**, not in any tool's session
(`Maestro/core/project-memory.md`):

- **`CLAUDE.md`** (this file) — stable rules.
- **`STATE.md`** — living state; this is where the handover happens between sessions and
  between people.
- **`product/`** — canonical artifacts (deep, lasting context).

Nothing relevant stays only in a session's ephemeral memory: if it matters to the next
session or to the team, **write it down**.

## 9. The framework (Maestro)

This project follows the **Maestro** framework, copied into `Maestro/` at the repository root
— a process reference, **read-only** during product development (it is not product code).
Full map: `Maestro/README.md`. Frequent entry points:

- `Maestro/core/orchestrator.md` — how the agents coordinate.
- `Maestro/core/lifecycle.md` — phases F0–F9 and what each one produces.
- `Maestro/agents/` — specialists by category, one per responsibility.
- `Maestro/workflows/` — processes that connect agents phase by phase.
- `Maestro/adapters/` — concrete mapping to the AI tool in use (Claude Code,
  Cowork, other).

Framework version copied: {{version — see `Maestro/_meta/VERSION.md`}}. If the framework
evolves in the origin repository, it is updated here deliberately (never by drift) and
recorded in `STATE.md`.

